ggml-vulkan: the Vulkan loader is opened at run time, not linked

EuLLM's CUDA build carries the Vulkan backend too, so that a card of another vendor beside an NVIDIA
one is used (an RTX 5070 Ti on CUDA and a Radeon RX 6700 XT on Vulkan: QwQ-32B Q4_K_M from 4.6 to
20.5 tokens/s, 24-11-2026). Linked, the loader (libvulkan.so.1, vulkan-1.dll) is needed for the
program to start at all, and CUDA containers, servers and HPC nodes often have none.

The backend already reaches Vulkan through vulkan-hpp's dynamic dispatcher. Its one entry point,
vkGetInstanceProcAddr, now comes from vulkan-hpp's DynamicLoader, which opens the loader at run
time; the backend's other direct calls (vkGetInstanceProcAddr, vkGetDeviceProcAddr,
vkGetPhysicalDeviceFeatures2, vkCmdCopyBuffer) go through the dispatcher, and VK_NO_PROTOTYPES
keeps any new one from compiling. Without a loader the instance
init throws, ggml_backend_vk_reg() returns no backend, and the program runs on its other backends.
CMake links Vulkan's headers only, and dl for dlopen.

EuLLM patch on llama.cpp b12632+23 (969d733).

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/CMakeLists.txt b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/CMakeLists.txt
